{"parentUuid":"4c22f865-0e6e-4c47-b1ba-6d6e25a212e4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZYUaXhM3ACrCZEdi2ir","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0113ufCdsHQfogpMSrTccoYG","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills","prompt":"How do you disable or turn off a skill via settings.json (e.g. skillOverrides, disabledSkills, permissions deny Skill(name))? Can a user skill override a bundled skill like /loop? Can SKILL.md frontmatter set model? Quote exact setting names and syntax."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":830,"cache_read_input_tokens":87973,"output_tokens":181,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":830,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":181,"cache_read_input_tokens":87973,"cache_creation_input_tokens":830,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":830},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0113ufCdsHQfogpMSrTccoYG":{"url":"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills","prompt":"How do you disable or turn off a skill via settings.json (e.g. skillOverrides, disabledSkills, permissions deny Skill(name))? Can a user skill override a bundled skill like /loop? Can SKILL.md frontmatter set model? Quote exact setting names and syntax."}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgZYUaJ4dE76NX8fpLTNM","requestRef":"9a1d8911-1fba-4d09-990c-51b845a8d460","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c86ef158-bf17-44ba-9f5b-48259422d7f1","timestamp":"2026-10-31T02:41:42.093Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","version":"2.1.314","gitBranch":"main","slug":"replicated-sleeping-unicorn"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","hash":"b03135e97403db484892aecb54356b595df3db6d6d1b4c3ff54b6a4a13cca234","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0113ufCdsHQfogpMSrTccoYG","type":"tool_result","content":"## Turning off a skill in settings\n\n**`skillOverrides`** is the setting for hiding or restricting a skill without editing its `SKILL.md`. Each key is a skill name, and each value is one of four states:\n\n| Value | Listed to Claude | In `/` menu |\n| :- | :- | :- |\n| `\"on\"` | Name and description | Yes |\n| `\"name-only\"` | Name only | Yes |\n| `\"user-invocable-only\"` | Hidden | Yes |\n| `\"off\"` | Hidden | Hidden |\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skillOverrides\": {\n    \"legacy-context\": \"name-only\",\n    \"deploy\": \"off\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nA skill missing from `skillOverrides` is treated as `\"on\"`. The `/skills` menu writes this setting for you: highlight a skill, press `Space` to cycle states, then press `Esc` to save to `.claude/settings.local.json`. Plugin skills aren't affected, so manage those through `/plugin`.\n\n**Permission deny rules** block Claude from invoking skills through the Skill tool:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"permissions\": {\n    \"deny\": [\n      \"Skill\",\n      \"Skill(deploy *)\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- `Skill` denies all skills.\n- `Skill(name)` matches the exact name. `Skill(name *)` matches the name with any arguments.\n\nThe content doesn't show the JSON wrapper for these rules. The `permissions.deny` placement is the standard permissions format.\n\n**`disabledSkills`** isn't mentioned in the provided documentation, so I can't confirm it exists or how it works.\n\n**Bundled skills** can be turned off all at once with `\"disableBundledSkills\": true`.\n\n**Frontmatter** can also hide a skill from Claude with `disable-model-invocation: true`, which still lets you invoke it with `/name`.\n\n## Can a user skill override `/loop`?\n\nYes, with a caveat. A personal, project, or enterprise skill with the same name replaces the bundled command, but not its aliases. The docs give this example: a project `code-review` skill replaces `/code-review`, and the bundled alias `/review` never runs your skill. A skill named `loop` would therefore replace `/loop`. Enterprise skills take precedence over personal ones, and personal ones over project ones.\n\n## Can frontmatter set `model`?\n\nYes. The `model` field sets the model for the skill:\n\n```yaml\n---\nname: quick-summary\ndescription: Summarize the current diff quickly\nmodel: haiku\n---\n```\n\n- It accepts the same values as `/model`, or `inherit` to keep the active model.\n- The override lasts for the current turn only and isn't saved to settings. The session model resumes with your next prompt.\n- If your organization's `availableModels` allowlist excludes the value, the session keeps its current model.\n- With `context: fork`, the value sets the forked subagent's model instead.\n\n[WebFetch note: this page's text is 118821 characters long and the answer above covers only characters 0 to 100000; the final 18821 were not read — to read on, call WebFetch again with the same url and offset: 100000.]"}]}}
