{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","hash":"46fe838c03fb85e8427db6073cddb52853dd8d8dcdeba157984d363bd737075b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015FrEW17XREfEU9YSv3iFVF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.claude; ls -lt --time-style=+%F projects/*/*.jsonl | tail -1 | awk '{print \"oldest transcript:\",$6}'; grep -n cleanupPeriodDays settings.json; python3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('settings.json'));print('keys:',list(d));print('skillOverrides:',d.get('skillOverrides'));print('disableBundled:',d.get('disableBundledSkills'))\"; ls .claude 2>/dev/null; ls ~/nexus-code/.claude/skills 2>/dev/null; cd skills; n=0; for d in */; do f=\"$d/SKILL.md\"; [ -f \"$f\" ] || continue; nm=$(awk '/^---/{c++;next} c==1 && /^name:/{sub(/^name:[ ]*/,\"\");gsub(/[\"'\"'\"']/,\"\");print;exit}' \"$f\"); echo \"${nm:-${d%/}}\"; done | sort -u > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403/scratchpad/skillnames.txt; wc -l < /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403/scratchpad/skillnames.txt; for d in */; do [ -f \"$d/SKILL.md\" ] || echo \"no SKILL.md: $d\"; done | head","description":"Check settings, transcript age, and collect personal skill names"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","hash":"453495e55859f06455aefa656e1e05c883a0c79cf855b72dc83d3cf796487b91","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Usage data covers Oct 2–31. Your only skill use in that window was `/loop`. Next I'm checking which subagents actually ran, then I'll show you the proposed changes."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JkZrwMnnjShfwJryLoyYkF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.claude; python3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('settings.json'));print(json.dumps(d.get('modelSettings'),indent=1));print(d.get('env'))\"; cd projects; find . -name '*.jsonl' -mtime -31 -print0 | xargs -0 grep -ho '\"description\":\"[^\"]\\{0,60\\}\",\"prompt\"[^}]\\{0,0\\}\\|\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\"[^}]\\{0,0\\}' | head -0; find . -name '*.jsonl' -mtime -31 -print0 | xargs -0 grep -h '\"name\":\"Agent\"' | grep -o '\"description\":\"[^\"]*\"[^{}]*\"subagent_type\":\"[^\"]*\"\\|\"subagent_type\":\"[^\"]*\"[^{}]*\"description\":\"[^\"]*\"' | sed 's/\"prompt\":\"[^\"]*\"//' | grep -o '\"description\":\"[^\"]*\"\\|\"subagent_type\":\"[^\"]*\"\\|\"model\":\"[^\"]*\"' | paste -sd' ' | sed 's/\"description\"/\\n\"description\"/g' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -40","description":"Show model settings and subagent task descriptions"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","hash":"9acf092c8242add2ce948067bf04a130a7eb19080b77ebca4d159e5ff79bb108","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0139NMRUREDavtmLkmpWjN5b","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403/scratchpad; python3 - \"$S\" <<'EOF'\nimport json,sys\ns=sys.argv[1]\nnames=[l.strip() for l in open(f\"{s}/skillnames.txt\") if l.strip()]\nkeep={\"graphify\",\"browse\"}\njson.dump({\"skillOverrides\":{n:\"off\" for n in names if n not in keep}},open(f\"{s}/skillOverrides.json\",\"w\"),indent=2)\nprint(len(names), [n for n in names if n in keep])\nEOF","description":"Draft skillOverrides block into scratchpad"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","hash":"b038753723152a3ae2c7696b5aee8336fb243c741ff1c0ea7dfca582f16cb484","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed anything yet. Below is each proposed change and what it would touch.\n\n**1. Cheaper model for search and lookup agents: nothing to change in your agent files**\nNone of your 10 custom agents in `~/.claude/agents/` is a search or lookup agent. All 10 plan, write code, test, review or audit.\n- `architect` and `orchestrator` use Opus; `coder` sets no model, so it inherits Opus; the other seven use Sonnet.\n- Over the last month the only one that actually ran was `reviewer`, 10 times. The other subagent runs were the built-in `general-purpose` (42) and `Explore` (4), and both are configured outside your agents folder.\n- I'd skip this item. The one real lookup agent is the built-in `Explore`, and I could try a `~/.claude/agents/Explore.md` with `model: haiku` to override it. I haven't confirmed that a custom agent can replace a built-in one, so I'd only do it if you want me to try and check.\n\n**2. `/loop`: new file `~/.claude/skills/loop/SKILL.md`**\n`/loop` is a built-in skill, so there's no SKILL.md of yours to edit. A personal skill with the same name replaces the built-in one. Proposed content:\n```markdown\n---\nname: loop\ndescription: Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo). Omit the interval to self-pace. Do NOT invoke for one-off tasks.\nmodel: sonnet\n---\n# /loop\nParse input as `[interval] <prompt>`: a first token matching ^\\d+[smhd]$ is the interval; else a trailing `every <N> <unit>` (only when a time follows \"every\"); else no interval (dynamic). Empty prompt → print `/loop [interval] <prompt>` and stop.\n\n## Fixed interval\nCron: Nm≤59 → `*/N * * * *`; Nm≥60 or Nh → `0 */H * * *`; Nd → `0 0 */N * *`; Ns → round up to minutes. Round uneven intervals to the nearest clean one and say so. CronCreate (recurring: true), confirm cadence + job ID in one line (expires after 7 days; cancel with CronDelete), then run the prompt now.\n\n## Dynamic\n1. Run the prompt now (slash command → Skill tool).\n2. If the next run waits on an event, arm one Monitor (timeout_ms 1800000) unless TaskList shows one running.\n3. If work remains: ScheduleWakeup with prompt `/loop <original input>`, delaySeconds 1200–1800 unless something specific changes sooner, noop true when nothing changed. Re-arming is a choice, not a default.\n4. Confirm in one short visible line.\n5. To stop: ScheduleWakeup stop:true, TaskStop any Monitor, one-line PushNotification (skip if the user asked to stop), then write the outcome.\n```\n- **Model:** `model: sonnet` applies to every iteration, because each wakeup re-enters `/loop`. This is where most of the savings come from. The catch is that your Nexus release loop, the 349 `/loop` runs, would do its review and diagnosis work on Sonnet instead of Opus. I'd use Sonnet rather than Haiku for that kind of work.\n- **Fewer steps:** I dropped the \"offer a cloud schedule\" step for intervals of an hour or more, and shortened the instructions.\n- **Subagents:** the loop skill itself starts none. The subagents in those runs came from your Nexus loop's own instructions; `reviewer` already uses Sonnet.\n\n**3. Turn off unused skills: add a `skillOverrides` block to `~/.claude/settings.json`**\n- **What counts as unused:** your transcripts cover Oct 2–31. In that time you used no personal skill by command or by Claude invoking it. The only skill used was `/loop`.\n- **What gets turned off:** all 277 personal skills in `~/.claude/skills/` would be set to `\"off\"`, which hides them from Claude and from the `/` menu.\n- **Two exceptions:** `graphify` and `browse` stay on, because your CLAUDE.md files tell me to use them.\n- **The full block** is in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403/scratchpad/skillOverrides.json`. I'd merge it in without touching your other settings.\n- **What it doesn't cover:**\n  - **Plugin skills** (`claude-mem:*`, `honcho:*`, `design:*`, `anthropic-skills:*` and others) aren't affected by this setting. You manage those with `/plugin`.\n  - **Built-in skills** that also went unused (`code-review`, `simplify`, `schedule` and others) stay on unless you want them in the block too.\n\nReply with which to apply: 2, 3, or both. You can also change any part, such as `haiku` instead of `sonnet`, keeping the cloud-schedule step, or adding the built-in skills to the block."}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","hash":"ba534c1fb41638966908a55da50c01ac67600e096f954d8d952a557e5d560037","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've made both changes.\n\n- **`/loop`:** your own version is at `~/.claude/skills/loop/SKILL.md` and is already being used in place of the built-in one. Each loop iteration now runs on Sonnet. I haven't run a loop with it yet.\n- **Unused skills:** `~/.claude/settings.json` now has a `skillOverrides` block that turns off 275 personal skills. `graphify` and `browse` are still on, and the new `loop` skill isn't in the block. I compared the rest of the file before and after, and nothing else changed.\n\nThe skills I turned off should drop out of the `/` menu in your next session, or after `/restart`. To turn one back on, delete its entry from the block or use `/skills`.\n\nA backup of the old settings file is at `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403/scratchpad/settings.json.bak`. That folder is temporary and only exists for this session.\n\nPlugin skills and built-in skills are unchanged, as discussed."}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","hash":"0251acb70b74d5ba4bb6de60c84bc399d9b57eddfe1aee2fef5ca713d1ebf131","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nAttribution for git commits and pull requests you create from here on (this replaces Claude Code's own earlier attribution guidance, such as a previous copy of this reminder; the user's own instructions about these lines, such as a CLAUDE.md or memory rule, take precedence over this reminder, but do not add attribution lines this reminder leaves out):\n- End git commit messages with:\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n- End pull request descriptions with:\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n</system-reminder>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<command-name>/restart</command-name>\n<command-message>restart</command-message>\n<command-args></command-args>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<local-command-stdout>Session resumed</local-command-stdout>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<command-message>loop</command-message>\n<command-name>/loop</command-name>\n<command-args>drive work actively to v1.0.0 release.</command-args>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Base directory for this skill: /home/mike/.claude/skills/loop\n\n# /loop\nParse input as `[interval] <prompt>`: a first token matching ^\\d+[smhd]$ is the interval; else a trailing `every <N> <unit>` (only when a time follows \"every\"); else no interval (dynamic). Empty prompt → print `/loop [interval] <prompt>` and stop.\n\n## Fixed interval\nCron: Nm≤59 → `*/N * * * *`; Nm≥60 or Nh → `0 */H * * *`; Nd → `0 0 */N * *`; Ns → round up to minutes. Round uneven intervals to the nearest clean one and say so. CronCreate (recurring: true), confirm cadence + job ID in one line (expires after 7 days; cancel with CronDelete), then run the prompt now.\n\n## Dynamic\n1. Run the prompt now (slash command → Skill tool).\n2. If the next run waits on an event, arm one Monitor (timeout_ms 1800000) unless TaskList shows one running.\n3. If work remains: ScheduleWakeup with prompt `/loop <original input>`, delaySeconds 1200–1800 unless something specific changes sooner, noop true when nothing changed. Re-arming is a choice, not a default.\n4. Confirm in one short visible line.\n5. To stop: ScheduleWakeup stop:true, TaskStop any Monitor, one-line PushNotification (skip if the user asked to stop), then write the outcome.\n\n\nARGUMENTS: drive work actively to v1.0.0 release."}]}}
