{"parentUuid":"3be20839-6610-4401-94b1-285fe8a32a18","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZut2NHhtUMSAQKhCHgr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G9gGKK5M3thhtaqgUZU7Nm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403/scratchpad/c360.md <<'EOF'\n### Release blocker: this commit cannot pass `release.yml` — claude-code\n\n**Head:** `40343e56418937b844c749b21f95ac76050b025c` (parent `16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99`)\n\n- **Test result:** Node 22 job 124463380784 had exactly one failure: 2033 tests, 2030 passed, 1 failed. The failing test is `cli/test/upgrade_tui.test.ts`, \"handles /upgrade --check via routeSlash\".\n- **Cause:** the mock's latest stable release is hard-coded as `v1.0.0`. Once the package itself says `1.0.0`, `/upgrade --check` correctly answers \"already up to date\", and the `/Update available/` assertion fails.\n- **Why fixing `main` doesn't help:** `release.yml` runs `npm --prefix cli test` on the checked-out **tag commit**. A tag on this commit therefore fails the release run whatever lands on `main`, #363 included. The stable cut has to be version-only on top of its RC, so the test fix can't be added here either.\n\n**Path forward:**\n1. Fix the fixture on `main`.\n2. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.15` with the fix included. It also carries #359's TUI change, which this commit lacks.\n3. Rebuild the stable commit as version-only on top of rc.15. The rc.14 gate evidence then needs an explicit, reviewed carry-forward to rc.15.\n\nThe draft hold stays correct regardless.\nEOF\ncat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403/scratchpad/c363.md <<'EOF'\n### Independent review: `CHANGES_REQUIRED` — claude-code\n\n**Head:** `450a8b3bba0f3afbc5c045be9d0de7f6746c1f47`\n\nThis change weakens the assertion. At stable `1.0.0`, `/Update available|already up to date/` no longer checks that `/upgrade --check` detects a newer release, which is the behavior this test exists to cover. The defect is in the fixture: its \"newer stable\" release is `v1.0.0`, so it stops being newer once the package version reaches 1.0.0.\n\n**Requested fix:**\n- Keep `/Update available/`.\n- Make the mock target strictly newer than any version under test, for example `v1.0.1`.\n- Update the dependent literals to match: target, archive name, VERSION, `--version` stubs, compatibility metadata, and `targetVersion` at :207.\n\n**Required verification:** the test passes with the cli version set to both `1.0.0-rc.14` and `1.0.0`.\n\n**Note for #360:** this fix has to ship in an RC. `release.yml` tests the tag tree, and the stable commit is version-only on top of its RC (see the comment on #360).\nEOF\nS=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403/scratchpad\ngh pr comment 360 --body-file $S/c360.md && gh pr comment 363 --body-file $S/c363.md && printf '%s\\n' \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) STATUS agent=claude-code finding=PR360_stable_on_rc14_fails_release_suite cause=upgrade_tui_fixture_latest_v1.0.0_equals_package_version job=124463380784 tests=2033_fail1 release.yml_tests_tag_tree=true implication=test_fix_needs_rc15_then_version_only_stable_on_rc15_with_reviewed_carry_forward REDACTED head=450a8b3b no_merge_no_tag\" >> .git/nexus-claims.log && echo logged","description":"Post findings on PRs 360 and 363 and log them"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1655,"cache_read_input_tokens":121008,"output_tokens":1804,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":309},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1655,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1804,"cache_read_inpu