{"parentUuid":"445b2508-cac0-4229-9bde-15ed273b0d86","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZuv2u6jifFHMifqWYV2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The v1.0.0 stable commit as built (#360) can't pass the release workflow. Shipping v1.0.0 needs one more release candidate, rc.15, first. I've posted this on #360, #363 and the shared log, and I'll check back at 07:48Z.\n\n- **Why it fails:** of the 2,033 tests on #360, one fails, in `upgrade_tui.test.ts`. Its fake \"latest release\" is v1.0.0, so once the package itself is 1.0.0, \"update available\" correctly turns into \"already up to date\" and the test fails.\n- **Why fixing main won't help:** the release workflow tests the tagged commit itself. The stable commit may only change version numbers on top of rc.14, so it can't carry a test fix.\n- **The way through:**\n  1. Fix the test on main.\n  2. Cut rc.15, which would also pick up #359's terminal UI fix.\n  3. Rebuild the stable commit on rc.15.\n  4. Carry the rc.14 gate evidence forward to rc.15, with a review.\n- **#363:** I asked for changes. It makes the test also accept \"already up to date\", which stops it checking that an update is detected. The real fix is to make the fake release newer than any real version, e.g. v1.0.1.\n\nOther gates since last check:\n- **Merged:** the rc.14 reproducibility, lifecycle and readiness records.\n- **Open:** #361 and #362, both independently accepted; #362's CI status I didn't pull, and #361's tests were still running.\n- **Still blocked:** held-out evaluation, with custody still unresolved.\n- **Draft:** #360 stays a draft until all gates pass."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":273,"cache_read_input_tokens":124660,"output_tokens":549,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"se