{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","hash":"481c7923799441b0686444b16d496f88106165ef69d24716ba0ecd7b6841df76","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QHmRNtA8t9sJHpkV97xY2y","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-code && for n in 360 363 361; do echo \"=== #$n\"; gh pr view $n --json headRefOid,baseRefName,author,isDraft,mergeable,body,commits --jq '\"head \\(.headRefOid) draft=\\(.isDraft) mergeable=\\(.mergeable)\\ncommits: \\([.commits[]|.oid[0:8]+\" parents?\"]|join(\",\"))\\n\\(.body[0:900])\"'; gh pr checks $n 2>&1 | awk -F'\\t' '{print $1\": \"$2}' | head -8; gh pr view $n --json comments --jq '.comments[]|select(.author.login!=\"coderabbitai\")|\"\\(.createdAt) \\(.body[0:300])\"' | tail -3; done; git log --format='%h %p %s' -3 origin/pr/360 2>/dev/null; git fetch origin pull/360/head:refs/tmp/pr360 -q && git log --format='%H parents=%P %s' -3 refs/tmp/pr360 && git diff --stat 16eeb6ee refs/tmp/pr360 | tail -15; grep -n \"HELDOUT\\|held-out\\|heldout\" .git/nexus-claims.log | tail -4 | cut -c1-300","description":"Inspect stable-promotion PR 360 and related PRs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","hash":"2cb6fc663924eda6059de9d362941f46111970ba3abb063938dc35e802f37551","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TxwfbNGhmF36kySK5NA3AV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-code && run=$(gh pr checks 360 --json name,link --jq '.[]|select(.name==\"test-matrix (22)\")|.link' | grep -o 'job/[0-9]*' | cut -d/ -f2); echo job=$run; gh api --allow-escape-sequences repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/jobs/$run/logs 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"^.*(not ok|# fail|# pass|✖|failing)\" | sed 's/^[^ ]* //' | head -20","description":"Pull failing test names from PR 360 Node 22 job"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","hash":"9dd9e9b45661fe8a648e160d86fd58741fdb17d513daafff9858c2fcebadce47","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PyYWt8TfmYKri4BwQi5zKd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-code && git show refs/tmp/pr360:cli/test/upgrade_tui.test.ts | grep -n \"Update available\\|version\\|latest\\|tag_name\\|1\\.0\\.0\" | head -20; echo ---; grep -niE \"rc\\.?15|successor_candidate|PR360|PR363|stable_promot\" .git/nexus-claims.log | tail -8 | cut -c1-350","description":"Check upgrade_tui test version dependency and successor plans"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","hash":"6d0284d71f304f42e34568e8ce51ed2deff2e727af5997ba1812614cef3c0d28","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found a blocker on the stable promotion PR (#360). Its only CI failure is a test that breaks once the version reads 1.0.0. I'm checking the proposed fix (#363) before I post findings."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BVMcyDaYKtFiGJDoKgCVao","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-code && gh pr diff 363 | head -30; git show refs/tmp/pr360:cli/test/upgrade_tui.test.ts | sed -n 14,40p; git show refs/tmp/pr360:cli/test/upgrade_tui.test.ts | sed -n 140,155p; grep -n \"npm --prefix cli test\\|checkout\" .github/workflows/release.yml | head","description":"Read PR 363 diff and the test fixture"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","hash":"c40a87888ea3c23fe420028f7c71c8f306240bc6c17012f51c0410a2d9a68360","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G9gGKK5M3thhtaqgUZU7Nm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-code && cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403/scratchpad/c360.md <<'EOF'\n### Release blocker: this commit cannot pass `release.yml` — claude-code\n\n**Head:** `40343e56418937b844c749b21f95ac76050b025c` (parent `16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99`)\n\n- **Test result:** Node 22 job 124463380784 had exactly one failure: 2033 tests, 2030 passed, 1 failed. The failing test is `cli/test/upgrade_tui.test.ts`, \"handles /upgrade --check via routeSlash\".\n- **Cause:** the mock's latest stable release is hard-coded as `v1.0.0`. Once the package itself says `1.0.0`, `/upgrade --check` correctly answers \"already up to date\", and the `/Update available/` assertion fails.\n- **Why fixing `main` doesn't help:** `release.yml` runs `npm --prefix cli test` on the checked-out **tag commit**. A tag on this commit therefore fails the release run whatever lands on `main`, #363 included. The stable cut has to be version-only on top of its RC, so the test fix can't be added here either.\n\n**Path forward:**\n1. Fix the fixture on `main`.\n2. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.15` with the fix included. It also carries #359's TUI change, which this commit lacks.\n3. Rebuild the stable commit as version-only on top of rc.15. The rc.14 gate evidence then needs an explicit, reviewed carry-forward to rc.15.\n\nThe draft hold stays correct regardless.\nEOF\ncat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403/scratchpad/c363.md <<'EOF'\n### Independent review: `CHANGES_REQUIRED` — claude-code\n\n**Head:** `450a8b3bba0f3afbc5c045be9d0de7f6746c1f47`\n\nThis change weakens the assertion. At stable `1.0.0`, `/Update available|already up to date/` no longer checks that `/upgrade --check` detects a newer release, which is the behavior this test exists to cover. The defect is in the fixture: its \"newer stable\" release is `v1.0.0`, so it stops being newer once the package version reaches 1.0.0.\n\n**Requested fix:**\n- Keep `/Update available/`.\n- Make the mock target strictly newer than any version under test, for example `v1.0.1`.\n- Update the dependent literals to match: target, archive name, VERSION, `--version` stubs, compatibility metadata, and `targetVersion` at :207.\n\n**Required verification:** the test passes with the cli version set to both `1.0.0-rc.14` and `1.0.0`.\n\n**Note for #360:** this fix has to ship in an RC. `release.yml` tests the tag tree, and the stable commit is version-only on top of its RC (see the comment on #360).\nEOF\nS=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403/scratchpad\ngh pr comment 360 --body-file $S/c360.md && gh pr comment 363 --body-file $S/c363.md && printf '%s\\n' \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ) STATUS agent=claude-code finding=PR360_stable_on_rc14_fails_release_suite cause=upgrade_tui_fixture_latest_v1.0.0_equals_package_version job=124463380784 tests=2033_fail1 release.yml_tests_tag_tree=true implication=test_fix_needs_rc15_then_version_only_stable_on_rc15_with_reviewed_carry_forward REDACTED head=450a8b3b no_merge_no_tag\" >> .git/nexus-claims.log && echo logged","description":"Post findings on PRs 360 and 363 and log them"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","hash":"cb65c505a482f307847033d088fdf6248c6370e96ce6b5dec07c1581693363cf","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nAttribution for git commits and pull requests you create from here on (this replaces Claude Code's own earlier attribution guidance, such as a previous copy of this reminder; the user's own instructions about these lines, such as a CLAUDE.md or memory rule, take precedence over this reminder, but do not add attribution lines this reminder leaves out):\n- End git commit messages with:\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n- End pull request descriptions with:\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n</system-reminder>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<command-message>loop</command-message>\n<command-name>/loop</command-name>\n<command-args>drive work actively to v1.0.0 release.</command-args>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Base directory for this skill: /home/mike/.claude/skills/loop\n\n# /loop\nParse input as `[interval] <prompt>`: a first token matching ^\\d+[smhd]$ is the interval; else a trailing `every <N> <unit>` (only when a time follows \"every\"); else no interval (dynamic). Empty prompt → print `/loop [interval] <prompt>` and stop.\n\n## Fixed interval\nCron: Nm≤59 → `*/N * * * *`; Nm≥60 or Nh → `0 */H * * *`; Nd → `0 0 */N * *`; Ns → round up to minutes. Round uneven intervals to the nearest clean one and say so. CronCreate (recurring: true), confirm cadence + job ID in one line (expires after 7 days; cancel with CronDelete), then run the prompt now.\n\n## Dynamic\n1. Run the prompt now (slash command → Skill tool).\n2. If the next run waits on an event, arm one Monitor (timeout_ms 1800000) unless TaskList shows one running.\n3. If work remains: ScheduleWakeup with prompt `/loop <original input>`, delaySeconds 1200–1800 unless something specific changes sooner, noop true when nothing changed. Re-arming is a choice, not a default.\n4. Confirm in one short visible line.\n5. To stop: ScheduleWakeup stop:true, TaskStop any Monitor, one-line PushNotification (skip if the user asked to stop), then write the outcome.\n\n\nARGUMENTS: drive work actively to v1.0.0 release."}]}}
