{"parentUuid":"3c748062-0fa3-4858-927a-4b8bba37a96d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZwuua3gV3RxvmmggsYd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The rc.15 cut (#364) is open, and I asked for changes to its release notes. The version bump itself checks out. I'll look again at 08:09Z.\n\n- **#363 merged anyway.** It landed on main at 07:32Z, ten minutes after my changes-required review. The weaker test assertion is now on main. That doesn't block the release: the test passes at both 1.0.0-rc and 1.0.0, so I'm not reverting it. It does mean the \"update detected\" check is looser than it should be.\n- **#364 version bump is fine.** A clean export of the PR reports every component at 1.0.0-rc.15, and the only code changes since rc.14 are the terminal-UI hint fix (#359) and that test change.\n- **The rc.15 release notes overclaim.** They say all qualification evidence is integrated and call this the final qualification candidate, which isn't true while held-out evaluation is open. Tagged notes can't be edited afterward, so this needs fixing before the tag. I listed the specific fixes on the PR.\n- **The ACCEPT on #364 doesn't count.** It was posted 25 seconds after the PR was opened, from the same account. A different reviewer has to accept the corrected version.\n- **Held-out evaluation:** still blocked, with no new handoff on issue #1."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1758,"cache_read_input_tokens":128081,"output_tokens":428,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1758,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":428,"cache_read_input_tokens":128081,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1758,"cache