{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"90831ce7-12dd-4e3f-a07d-bc2921efe403","hash":"de8d62e6d969c91ece932d3ba1f0b66dd896b3a0eb9118c862a1bc3806a34fa6","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018xeeEgqqP8BMQj1FMNmFyV","type":"tool_result","content":"exit=0\n---366\n2026-10-31T10:53:58Z\n## Summary\n\n- Keep speculative worktree task IDs for tool authority and execution receipts.\n- Record durable operation start/end events against the parent session task ID, which is the identity initialized and retained by checkpoints.\n- Add a regression assertion to the interactive worktree lifecycle test for both journal calls.\n\nThis fixes the RC15 standalone synthetic task where operation journaling targeted a worktree ID with no durable state record, causing a correct externally validated patch to remain `REGRESSION_FREE` instead of being deliverable-bound and durable.\n\n## Validation\n\n- CLI TypeScript build: pass.\n- `harness-core` debug build: pass.\n- Focused `harness.test.ts` worktree lifecycle test: 1/1 pass with isolated HOME.\n- `git diff --check`: pass.\n- Exact-head CI and independent review: pending.\n\nThis source fix does not retroactively qualify RC15 or constitute exact-RC acce\n cli/src/agent.ts | 13 +++++++++----\n 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]}}
